@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #000000
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #000000
skinparam ComponentFontColor #000000
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #000000
skinparam RectangleFontColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseFontColor #000000

title Product Operating Model Before PM Toolkit Expansion

actor "LLM / Agent" as Agent #E8F0FE
component "Product Management Engine" as Engine #D0E0FF
component "Backlog Analyzer\nstale + cycle ranking" as Analyzer #D9EAD3
component "Signal Vetting Gate\nconfidence + evidence" as Vetting #FFF4CC
component "Issue Creation\nLinear / GitHub" as Creator #FCE5CD
database "Linear + GitHub Work" as Work #EAF7EA

Agent --> Engine : analyze backlog\nor create proactive issues
Engine --> Analyzer : score live work
Analyzer --> Work : read issues and cycles
Engine --> Vetting : check signal fields
Vetting --> Creator : qualified signal
Creator --> Work : create templated issue

note bottom of Engine #FFFDEB
The engine can find stale work and vet signals,
but PM discipline is still shallow:
metrics, guardrails, kill criteria,
portfolio allocation, and roadmap scoring
are not enforced as first-class outputs.
end note

@enduml
